            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0524" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/382</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 718</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs of the Haitian Government, informs me
                    that in view <pb facs="0525" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/> of the recent exchange of
                    notes between the Haitian Minister at Washington and the Department of State,
                    the Claims Commission has been informed of the provisions of the Haitian-French
                    Agreement of June 12, 1925, for the regulations of the claims of French citizens
                    and those under French protection. He also informs me that the above named
                    agreement was sanctioned by the National Assembly in the session of February 17,
                    1926.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John H. Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
